      "side": 1,
      "message": "`vector-unfold!` (and `vector-unfold-right!`, 489) checks only that the indices are non-negative integers.\n\n- **Reversed range:** `(vector-unfold! f w 4 2)` silently does nothing.\n- **End past the vector:** `(vector-unfold! (lambda (i) \u0027x) v 1 5)` on `#(1 2 3)` raises only after storing, leaving `v` as `#(1 x x)`.\n- **Not a vector:** a non-vector is accepted when the range is empty.\n\n`check-type vector?` and `check-indices` before the first store.",
      "revId": "b8ac22d5b0a55b684657d0706c0efe31172e334b",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
