      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T21:38:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "None of the triples is checked.\n\n- `(vector-append-subvectors (vector \u0027a \u0027b \u0027c \u0027d) 0 2 (vector \u0027d \u0027e \u0027f) 3 2 (vector \u0027x \u0027y) 0 1)` returns `#(a x)` instead of raising: start 3 \u003e end 2. A negative-length triple shrinks the total and moves the write position back, so the next subvector overwrites earlier output.\n- Other bad input fails with whatever error comes up first. A start of -1 gives a `vector-ref` range error, a flonum end gives a `make-vector` error, and an odd argument count gives \"cdr: expected a pair, got ()\".\n\nCheck each triple with `check-type vector?` and `check-indices`, and name the procedure for an odd count.",
      "revId": "b8ac22d5b0a55b684657d0706c0efe31172e334b",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
