      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T21:38:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The mutators here skip the project\u0027s literal-vector check: `vector-swap!`, `vector-reverse!` (1069), `vector-map!` (734), `vector-reverse-copy!` (1025), `vector-unfold!` (425) and `vector-unfold-right!` (469). literal-vectors-immutable.scm requires that \"every vector mutator raises\" on a literal, that \"an empty range still raises: the check comes before any store\", and that the message names the procedure. 132.sld meets this with `%check-mutable-vector`.\n\nHere `(vector-reverse! \u0027#(3 1 2) 1 1)` returns normally. Non-empty ranges raise \"vector-set!: the vector #(3 1 2) is immutable\", naming `vector-set!` rather than the procedure called, and `vector-map!` calls `f` once before that.\n\nImport `(only (vali primitive) %check-mutable-vector)` as 132.sld does, call it first in each mutator, and add these to that regression test (and 133.sld to ADR 0020 §7\u0027s table, beside 132).",
      "revId": "b8ac22d5b0a55b684657d0706c0efe31172e334b",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
